  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="7a23-008d-b13c-c95c" name="English Hundred Years War (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>HUNDRED YEARS WAR ENGLISH 1337-1453 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.14-15). Special rule The Herce: units of Archers within 4" of a unit or combined unit of Dismounted Knights or Dismounted Men-at-Arms may stand &amp; fire at chargers without the -1 penalty.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[English Hundred Years War - Continental]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 35%
  Archers: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 35%
  Continental Army (Crecy 1346, Agincourt 1415). Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 0-35%, Archers 25-50% (cannot have Poor Archers), Infantry 0-35% (cannot have Peasants). Artillery: up to 1 light artillery per 1,000 army points, bought from the Infantry allocation. Mercenaries: 0-20% from the Free Companies list (no characters or Artillery); all are subject to the Allies and Mercenaries rule (documented only).
[English Hundred Years War - Home]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 30%
  Archers: up to 40%, at least 20%
  Infantry: up to 40%
  Home Army (Shrewsbury 1403 and other battles in Britain). Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 0-30%, Archers 20-40% (must have 1+ unit of Poor Archers), Infantry 0-40% (cannot have Mercenary Handgunners). Artillery: up to 1 light artillery per 1,000 army points, bought from the Infantry allocation.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
